{"The message in printFeatureDisabled() hardcodes 'rolling-updates' while the enum uses ROLLING_UPDATES. If the key or display name changes, this will drift. Should derive the user-facing/config name from Profile.Feature (e.g., a property or helper) instead of embedding the string literal.": 0.15419894456863403, "Missing test for UpdateCompatibilityCheck when the feature is not enabled - the same feature gate exists in UpdateCompatibilityCheck.run() without a corresponding test. Need to add a @Launch({UpdateCompatibility.NAME, UpdateCompatibilityCheck.NAME}) test that verifies the same error message and exit code.": 0.2702106535434723, "The feature-enabled guard for rolling updates is duplicated in both UpdateCompatibilityCheck.run() and UpdateCompatibilityMetadata.run(); could move this into a shared helper in AbstractUpdatesCommand to reduce duplication and ensure consistent behavior.": 0.07528495043516159, "In UpgradeTest.createInitialDeployment, setting kc.getSpec().getFeatureSpec().setEnabledFeatures(List.of(...)) will overwrite any previously configured enabled features; if other features may already be set on the spec, consider appending the rolling-updates feature instead of replacing the list.": 0.09560275822877884}